• Yes. The frontend is relying on a set of backend flags/status fields to drive UI state. Some already exist, some are inferred, and some should become
  explicit instead of being guessed.

  The important ones are these.

  Transactions
  You already have most of this, but these flags matter directly:

  - status
      - expected values: categorized, to_review, pending, excluded

  - includedInCashFlow
      - boolean

  - type
      - expected values: income, expense, transfer

  What to modify:

  - Transaction
      - today includedInCashFlow and notes live in metadata
      - better model:
          - add includedInCashFlow: Boolean
          - add notes: String

  - DTOs:
      - src/main/java/com/Accounting/app/dashboard/dto/TransactionsPageResponse.java
      - patch request DTO already exists:
          - src/main/java/com/Accounting/app/dashboard/dto/TransactionUpdateRequest.java

  Uploaded files / receipt workflow
  Frontend is using file lifecycle flags heavily.

  Needed flags:

  - status
      - expected values: uploaded, processing, extracted, needs review

  - fileType
      - expected values: image, pdf, spreadsheet

  - documentType
      - backend-facing: RECEIPT, SPREADSHEET, INVOICE, TAX_DOCUMENT, OTHER

  - previewUrl
  - fileUrl

  What to modify:

  - UploadedFile
      - keep status, but normalize values to frontend contract
      - add stronger explicit fields if you want less metadata parsing:
          - merchantName
          - documentDate
          - extractedAmount
          - extractedCategory
          - confidence
          - taxRelevance
          - maybe processingJobId

  - DTOs:
      - whatever DTO powers /api/dashboard/files and upload responses
      - likely src/main/java/com/Accounting/app/files/dto/UploadedFileDto.java and upload response DTOs

  Linked institutions
  Frontend wants connection-health flags, not just raw Plaid item data.

  Needed flags:

  - syncStatus
      - healthy, limited_access, needs_reconnect, syncing

  - productsEnabled[].enabled
      - boolean

  - connectionStatus
      - display string like Healthy

  - metrics flags are numeric, but statuses drive the UI

  What to modify:

  - PlaidItem
      - add explicit fields if you want this stable:
          - syncStatus
          - lastSuccessfulSyncAt
          - lastSyncAttemptAt
          - needsReconnect

  - DTOs:
      - src/main/java/com/Accounting/app/dashboard/dto/LinkedInstitutionsPageResponse.java

  Team access
  Flags here are simple but should be explicit.

  Needed flags:

  - member role
      - owner, admin, accountant, member, viewer

  - member status
      - active, invited, disabled

  - invitation status
      - pending, accepted, expired, revoked

  What to modify:

  - AppSettingsTeamMember
      - already has role, status

  - TeamInvitation
      - already has role, status

  - no major structural change needed unless you want accepted invites to become first-class team members in a real table

  Overview review queue
  Frontend uses these flags for badges and icons:

  - priority
      - High, Medium, Low

  - tone
      - examples: indigo, green, rose, amber

  - icon
      - examples: receipt, fileText, alertTriangle, sparkles

  What to modify:

  - DTO only:
      - src/main/java/com/Accounting/app/dashboard/dto/OverviewPageResponse.java

  - no entity change required unless review items become persistent workflow records

  Financial health / goals
  Needed flags:

  - goal status
      - on_track, needs_attention

  - alert severity
      - warning, info, success

  What to modify:

  - DTOs only unless goals become editable persistent records

  Expense breakdown
  Needed flags:

  - expenseDetails[].status
      - categorized, matched_receipt, needs_review

  What to modify:

  - DTO only right now
  - if you want this cleaner, add explicit linkage state between UploadedFile and Transaction

  Dividends / portfolio / holdings
  Mostly numeric, but a few status flags matter:

  - connectedAccounts[].status
      - synced, syncing, needs_attention

  - dividend history status
      - currently things like posted

  What to modify:

  - mostly DTOs
  - possibly PlaidItem / account sync fields if you want real sync-health state

  Tax documents page
  This is the big missing one if you build it next.

  Needed flags:

  - document status
      - page currently uses values like Ready, Needs Review, Processing, Missing Info

  - file type
      - pdf, excel

  - checks severity/count state

  What to modify:

  - either extend UploadedFile for tax docs, or create a dedicated TaxDocument entity
  - if you want this page done cleanly, I would create:
      - TaxDocument
      - TaxDocumentStatus
      - maybe TaxDocumentCheck



